  triage:title "Compatibility fixtures for pre-AJ snapshot (missing members field) / older-reader tolerance do not exist" ;
  triage:description "Sprint doc requires fixtures proving 'a new reader accepts a pre-AJ snapshot without members' and 'an older reader ignores the additive field.' The only relevant test, runtime_status_snapshot_round_trips (protocol.rs), round-trips a snapshot with members: Vec::new() on both sides -- never decodes a legacy JSON payload omitting the members key, unlike the adjacent legacy-compat pattern already used correctly for heartbeat_session_id. Confirmed by req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa-agent. QA source: PR #741, phase-aj-s6-qa-1." ;
